From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:40:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 016/342] device_manager: probe busses/usb for generic (device
 tree) nodes

Device tree nodes have no type, so the device manager only tries a fixed
list of module directories for them; busses/mmc is there, busses/usb was
not, so FDT-attached USB host controllers were never probed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/device_manager/device_manager.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/device_manager/device_manager.cpp b/src/system/kernel/device_manager/device_manager.cpp
index d06303c01f..0f6400c1b1 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/device_manager/device_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/device_manager/device_manager.cpp
@@ -1749,6 +1749,8 @@ device_node::_GetNextDriverPath(void*& cookie, KPath& _path)
 					_AddPath(*stack, "bus_managers/pci");
 					_AddPath(*stack, "busses/pci");
 					_AddPath(*stack, "busses/mmc");
+					_AddPath(*stack, "busses/usb");
+						// device tree attached USB host controllers
 				}
 				break;
 		}
